## TIẾNG ANH · 16:30–17:00 — Thứ Sáu: Nhìn lại tuần

### 16:30–16:40 · Shadowing

### 16:40–17:00 · Nói to có ghi âm — 3 phút

> **1. What I did**
> *"AI week. I built natural language meal entry and an assistant chat, both behind an authenticated Edge Function so the model key never reaches the device."*
>
> **2. The decision I'd defend hardest**
> *"Nothing saves automatically. The parse produces a preview the user confirms. The model is guessing at portion sizes and the user actually knows — and it means if the model fails, they just use the form, which is what they did before. The feature is an accelerator, not a dependency."*
>
> **3. What I chose not to do**
> *"I deliberately didn't use a model for anything deterministic. Summing calories is arithmetic. Using a non-deterministic, paid, slower tool for that would be a downgrade. I wrote that down, because I think knowing where not to use something is part of knowing how to use it."*
>
> **4. Next week**
> *"Push notifications and deep linking. Real push through FCM and APNs, and links that open the right screen even from a cold start."*

**Kiêm buổi họp một mình.** Tuần này thêm một câu hỏi: việc bắt đầu apply có làm tôi lo lắng nhiều hơn không? Nếu có, đó là bình thường — nhưng đừng để nó ăn vào giờ ngủ.

